eted  but not your home not the home of your  loved ones of your friends you don't  expect to spend your Saturday on the  phone constantly calling family from  asking whether whether they're alive or  not  and now Ukraine is poised to see  more Russian forces  are you worried about the direction of  the war well we are worried first of all  that there will be more missile strikes  in the coming days because we know from  intelligence that Russia has not  exhausted even half of their Arsenal  that was intended for these attacks and  we know that there is uh missile  launcher  cargo ships in the in the marine regions  ready to go so this is this is something  we are preparing the short term and the  long term of course and the midterm uh  it is expected that Russia will regroup  and will start relaunching the attacks  especially with spring when the calls  will be not so when it will not be so  difficult because of the call to to make  advancements and this is why Ukraine is  constantly on the ask for more weapons  and for these tanks as you just  mentioned that the UK will be sending  tanks Challenger tanks to Ukraine we are  extremely grateful for that and we are  hoping that Germany will see this as an  example to follow and will eventually  give way and give us the the tanks and  the armored vehicles we have been so  desperately asking for to have that uh  that benefit on the Battleground let's  talk about the tanks and because as you  say the UK is sending Challenger 2 tanks  the first time a western country has  pledged tanks how important is that uh  the fighting on the on the ground on the  eastern Southeastern Northeastern  Borders or contact line for Ukraine it's  crucial that we have artillery on the  ground it's crucial that we have tanks  on the ground because this is what  Russia is fighting us with so we need  this as defense vehicles but we also  need these as counter-offensive  instruments to push the Russians back  and it is crucial that we do this by the  end of spring that would get a pushback  of Russian forces beyond the Ukraine  Russian borders the 1991 Ukraine Russian  borders and that we secure the area with  with proper defense structures and  facilities and to do that we need these  uh these heavy weapons which are the  tanks you you said that you hope Germany  follows the UK's example do you think  that some countries  are not doing enough  uh while Germany being one of them I  mean they have these weapons sitting  there that they are not using and that  hopefully fingers crossed they will not  have to use because Ukraine will be  Victorious and will manage to fight off  the biggest aggressor in Europe so for  Germany not to have to use these tanks  they need to be in Ukraine on the ground  fighting and the same goes for every  single country who still has weapons and  the storage units and the storage houses  and is stalling from giving them to  Ukraine because the only threat in  Europe at this moment and one of the  largest threats to Security in the world  is Russia and the only country that can  physically stop Russia is Ukraine and we  are happy to do this on the ground  within our territory we are happy to  push back Russia within its borders but  we need the means to do it and this is  this is why the appeals from our  Minister of Defense from a foreign  minister from our president from every  single Ukrainian gave us weapons give us  the tanks give us the anti-air  weapons and systems that we need give us  the ammunition to go with are you it's  interesting isn't it because um you know  speaking to you today making these calls  is it often that women of Ukraine who  are having to come on programs like this  who are having to speak to the  politicians to travel the world because  the men are fighting it's definitely  easier for the women to cross the  borders even if we're talking about  women who are in politics who are in  people who are in politics or in  government positions it still is ea