lk  about something that is so familiar and  ordinary to so many people watching you  totally won't sleep so you take them in  the prams to try and take them outside  you know you want them to be quiet so  you put Peppa Pig on the phone  and yet it's in such an extraordinary  situation for a parent I I can't imagine  you know I talked to you as a politician  but also as a mother  um I just can't really grasp  what people in Ukraine are having to go  through uh you know neither can I  because it's just  um it just doesn't sit well with the  ordinary with the normal life of a  person living in the modern world  uh you cannot piece the puzzle together  and I think that after the victory after  Ukraine wins we will have a lot of  mending to do and a lot of healing to do  because all of these things which our  brain doesn't allow us really to  register and to grasp and what we are  actually doing uh they are going to  flood us and there's going to be a lot  of issues to deal with both for the  people who will be coming back from the  front lines as well as the people who  will be coming back from abroad as well  as the people who have had to stay and  live through these Air Raids because it  does feel like the whole of Ukraine it's  a front line the whole of Ukraine is a  Frontline and it's a fact and do you  think that you can win them absolutely  we have no other choice you have no  other choice we have to win this war for  uh democracy sake uh this is an  existential War for Ukraine it's  existential because we want to exist we  want to live so this is why we are  fighting but for uh people who are  supporting us for the UK for example  it's an existential War because it's  existential between good and evil who do  you want to and you won't get to win you  want the world to be a safe place you  don't want to be seeing pictures like  this on Sunday morning and you most  certainly don't want to be living  through pictures like this any day of  your life and in order for